Z||000002||hugh||11-04-2001||08:39 AM||||Chuck,You don't know what you just got into.I started buying the cars from Texaco,they were only about $16.It just overcame me after that.I started buying every Texaco piece I came across.Then I started to buy Franklin Mint and it only got worse.I used to get on Ebay as soon as I got home from work.Something started me into thinking about a different kind of car.I looked at Corvairs(I bought one new in 1963)and Fieros.I opted for Fieros because of this forum and haven't looked back.I stopped getting on Ebay and have probably saved thousands of dollars on diecast.Of course I've spent an ungodly amount of money on my car and time on here.But on here you can learn and grow and on Ebay you can only spend.Sorry for rambling,but that happens when you get old.At least I didn't forget what I was talking about.||||reg||1
